      "title": "Multiple Alleles & Polygenic Traits",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIIa-b-3",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Define multiple alleles.</li><li>Describe the ABO blood group system.</li><li>Define polygenic inheritance.</li><li>Give examples of polygenic traits.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Multiple alleles</strong> — more than two alleles in a population.</li><li><strong>ABO blood group</strong> — 3 alleles: Iᴬ, Iᴮ, i.</li><li><strong>Polygenic trait</strong> — controlled by multiple genes.</li><li><strong>Continuous variation</strong> — a range of phenotypes.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Multiple Alleles — ABO Blood Type</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Genotype</th><th>Blood Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>IᴬIᴬ or Iᴬi</td><td>A</td></tr><tr><td>IᴮIᴮ or Iᴮi</td><td>B</td></tr><tr><td>IᴬIᴮ</td><td>AB</td></tr><tr><td>ii</td><td>O</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>B. Polygenic Traits</h4><ul><li>Height, skin color, eye color</li><li>Show continuous variation</li><li>Each gene adds a small effect</li></ul><h4>C. Other Modifications</h4><ul><li><strong>Epistasis</strong> — one gene masks another</li><li><strong>Pleiotropy</strong> — one gene affects multiple traits</li></ul>",
      "activity1": {
