      "title": "DNA & RNA Structure",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIIa-b-4",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Describe the molecular structure of DNA.</li><li>Describe the structure of RNA.</li><li>Compare DNA and RNA.</li><li>Explain base pairing.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Nucleotide</strong> — sugar + phosphate + base.</li><li><strong>Double helix</strong> — DNA's twisted ladder structure.</li><li><strong>Base pairing</strong> — A–T, G–C (DNA); A–U, G–C (RNA).</li><li><strong>Antiparallel</strong> — strands run in opposite directions.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. DNA Structure</h4><ul><li>Double-stranded helix</li><li>Sugar: deoxyribose</li><li>Bases: A, T, G, C</li><li>Base pairing: A–T, G–C</li><li>Antiparallel strands</li></ul><h4>B. RNA Structure</h4><ul><li>Single-stranded</li><li>Sugar: ribose</li><li>Bases: A, U, G, C</li><li>Base pairing: A–U, G–C</li><li>Three types: mRNA, tRNA, rRNA</li></ul><h4>C. DNA vs RNA</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>DNA</th><th>RNA</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sugar</td><td>Deoxyribose</td><td>Ribose</td></tr><tr><td>Strands</td><td>Double</td><td>Single</td></tr><tr><td>Bases</td><td>A, T, G, C</td><td>A, U, G, C</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Genetic storage</td><td>Protein synthesis</td></tr></tbody></table>",
      "activity1": {
